{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definitions are plain objects with the following options:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"id","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"code","value":"id: string","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The unique identifier for the column."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧠 A column ID is optional when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An accessor column is created with an object key accessor"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The column header is defined as a string"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"accessorkey","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorKey"}]},{"type":"code","value":"accessorKey?: string & typeof TData","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key of the row object to use when extracting the value for the column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"accessorfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"accessorFn?: (originalRow: TData, index: number) => any","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The accessor function to use when extracting the value for the column from each row."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"columns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"columns?: ColumnDef<TData>[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The child column defs to include in a group column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"header","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"}]},{"type":"code","value":"header?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The header to display for the column. If a string is passed, it can be used as a default for the column ID. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the header and should return the rendered header value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"footer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"footer?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The footer to display for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the footer and should return the rendered footer value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"}]},{"type":"code","value":"cell?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      row: Row<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n      cell: Cell<TData>\n      getValue: () => any\n      renderValue: () => any\n    }) => unknown)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The cell to display each row for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the cell and should return the rendered cell value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"meta","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"}]},{"type":"code","value":"meta?: ColumnMeta // This interface is extensible via declaration merging. See below!","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The meta data to be associated with the column. We can access it anywhere when the column is available via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.columnDef.meta"},{"type":"text","value":". This type is global to all tables and can be extended like so:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import '@tanstack/react-table' //or vue, svelte, solid, qwik, etc.\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TData extends RowData, TValue> {\n    foo: string\n  }\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"id","text":"id","level":3},{"id":"accessorkey","text":"accessorKey","level":3},{"id":"accessorfn","text":"accessorFn","level":3},{"id":"columns","text":"columns","level":3},{"id":"header","text":"header","level":3},{"id":"footer","text":"footer","level":3},{"id":"cell","text":"cell","level":3},{"id":"meta","text":"meta","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nColumn definitions are plain objects with the following options:\n\n## Options\n\n### `id`\n\n```tsx\nid: string\n```\n\nThe unique identifier for the column.\n\n> 🧠 A column ID is optional when:\n>\n> - An accessor column is created with an object key accessor\n> - The column header is defined as a string\n\n### `accessorKey`\n\n```tsx\naccessorKey?: string & typeof TData\n```\n\nThe key of the row object to use when extracting the value for the column.\n\n### `accessorFn`\n\n```tsx\naccessorFn?: (originalRow: TData, index: number) => any\n```\n\nThe accessor function to use when extracting the value for the column from each row.\n\n### `columns`\n\n```tsx\ncolumns?: ColumnDef<TData>[]\n```\n\nThe child column defs to include in a group column.\n\n### `header`\n\n```tsx\nheader?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe header to display for the column. If a string is passed, it can be used as a default for the column ID. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the header and should return the rendered header value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `footer`\n\n```tsx\nfooter?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe footer to display for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the footer and should return the rendered footer value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `cell`\n\n```tsx\ncell?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      row: Row<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n      cell: Cell<TData>\n      getValue: () => any\n      renderValue: () => any\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe cell to display each row for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the cell and should return the rendered cell value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `meta`\n\n```tsx\nmeta?: ColumnMeta // This interface is extensible via declaration merging. See below!\n```\n\nThe meta data to be associated with the column. We can access it anywhere when the column is available via `column.columnDef.meta`. This type is global to all tables and can be extended like so:\n\n```tsx\nimport '@tanstack/react-table' //or vue, svelte, solid, qwik, etc.\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TData extends RowData, TValue> {\n    foo: string\n  }\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: ColumnDef APIs\n---\n\nColumn definitions are plain objects with the following options:\n\n## Options\n\n### `id`\n\n```tsx\nid: string\n```\n\nThe unique identifier for the column.\n\n> 🧠 A column ID is optional when:\n>\n> - An accessor column is created with an object key accessor\n> - The column header is defined as a string\n\n### `accessorKey`\n\n```tsx\naccessorKey?: string & typeof TData\n```\n\nThe key of the row object to use when extracting the value for the column.\n\n### `accessorFn`\n\n```tsx\naccessorFn?: (originalRow: TData, index: number) => any\n```\n\nThe accessor function to use when extracting the value for the column from each row.\n\n### `columns`\n\n```tsx\ncolumns?: ColumnDef<TData>[]\n```\n\nThe child column defs to include in a group column.\n\n### `header`\n\n```tsx\nheader?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe header to display for the column. If a string is passed, it can be used as a default for the column ID. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the header and should return the rendered header value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `footer`\n\n```tsx\nfooter?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      header: Header<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe footer to display for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the footer and should return the rendered footer value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `cell`\n\n```tsx\ncell?:\n  | string\n  | ((props: {\n      table: Table<TData>\n      row: Row<TData>\n      column: Column<TData>\n      cell: Cell<TData>\n      getValue: () => any\n      renderValue: () => any\n    }) => unknown)\n```\n\nThe cell to display each row for the column. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object for the cell and should return the rendered cell value (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `meta`\n\n```tsx\nmeta?: ColumnMeta // This interface is extensible via declaration merging. See below!\n```\n\nThe meta data to be associated with the column. We can access it anywhere when the column is available via `column.columnDef.meta`. This type is global to all tables and can be extended like so:\n\n```tsx\nimport '@tanstack/react-table' //or vue, svelte, solid, qwik, etc.\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-table' {\n  interface ColumnMeta<TData extends RowData, TValue> {\n    foo: string\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
